---
import ToolPage from '@versal/ui/ToolPage.astro';

const title = "URL Encoder & Decoder";
const description = "Percent-encode or decode URLs, query strings, form data and path segments. Supports full-URL and component encoding, plus hex and octal escapes. No upload.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How do I URL encode a string?",
    "answer": "Paste your text into the input and click Encode. Special characters like spaces, &, =, and ? are converted to percent-encoded form (%20, %26, etc.) safe for use in URLs. Click Decode to reverse the encoding."
  },
  {
    "question": "What characters are encoded?",
    "answer": "All characters not safe in URLs are encoded: spaces, quotes, angle brackets, hash, percent, and non-ASCII characters. Alphanumeric and -_.~ are left unchanged (RFC 3986 safe set)."
  }
];
import ToolNav from '@versal/ui/ToolNav.astro';
import BaseLayout from '@versal/ui/BaseLayout';
---

<ToolPage
  site="devops"
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://jsonversal.com/devops/tools/url-codec/"
  current="/devops/tools/url-codec/"
  faqs={faqs}
  about={[
    {
      "heading": "Two encoders, and the set each one spares",
      "body": [
        "The JavaScript unreserved set is `A-Za-z0-9-_.!~*'()` — note that `!~*'()` survive, which is slightly wider than the RFC 3986 unreserved set. `encodeURIComponent` escapes everything else, including `&`, `=`, `?`, `/` and `#`, which is what you want for a value destined for a query parameter. `encodeURI` preserves the reserved punctuation so the structure of a URL survives intact, which is what you want when the whole URL is the input.",
        "Choosing between them by position rather than by string: a query value goes through the component encoder, a full URL through the URI encoder, and pasting a full URL into component mode yields a single escaped token with every separator turned into `%26` or `%3F`. That output is technically a valid encoding of the whole string and completely wrong as a URL."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Spaces, plus signs, and double encoding",
      "body": [
        "A space becomes `%20` in both modes, and nothing here ever produces a `+`. That is correct for a query string under RFC 3986 and wrong for an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body, where a space is `+` and `decodeURIComponent` will not convert it back. Form posts decoded with this tool leave `+` sitting in the value, which is the single most common cause of a signature mismatch or a silently wrong query.",
        "Percent itself is encoded, so `%` becomes `%25`. Encoding a string that is already encoded is therefore not idempotent — a space that was `%20` is now `%2520` — and the failure compounds every round trip. The Swap button moves the output back into the input, which is the fastest way to see it: swap once and a correct value is unchanged, while a double-encoded one visibly grows."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Unicode expansion, malformed input, and where errors surface",
      "body": [
        "Non-ASCII characters are encoded as UTF-8 first and each byte then written as `%XX`, so a CJK character costs three bytes and becomes nine characters, and an emoji costs four bytes and twelve characters. The size readout counts UTF-16 code units rather than bytes, which means the expansion ratio for emoji is understated by half — the direction that matters when you are checking a URL against a length limit.",
        "Malformed input throws: a stray `%`, a truncated `%E4%B8`, or a lone `%ZZ` all raise a URIError from `decodeURIComponent`, and the message is written into the output box prefixed with `Error:` rather than into a separate status area — worth knowing before you copy the output. There is no `decodeURI` mode, so decoding a whole URL with the component decoder also turns `%3F` and `%26` back into live delimiters, handing you a string that no longer parses as the URL it came from."
      ]
    }
  ]}
>

  <div class="card mt-2">
    <div class="row" style="gap:8px;margin-bottom:12px;">
      <label class="text-muted" for="mode">Mode</label>
      <select id="mode">
        <option value="encode">Encode (encodeURIComponent)</option>
        <option value="encodeURI">Encode full URL (encodeURI)</option>
        <option value="decode" selected>Decode</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;">
      <div>
        <strong>Input</strong>
        <label for="input" class="sr-only">Input</label>
        <textarea id="input" spellcheck="false" placeholder='https://example.com/path?q=hello world&name=ada' style="min-height:180px;margin-top:8px;"></textarea>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Output</strong>
        <label for="output" class="sr-only">Output</label>
        <textarea id="output" spellcheck="false" readonly placeholder='Result appears here' style="min-height:180px;margin-top:8px;background:var(--surface-2);"></textarea>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row mt-1" style="gap:8px;">
      <button class="primary" id="run">Run</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="swap">Swap</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="copy">Copy output</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="clear">Clear</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card mt-2" id="stats" style="display:none;">
    <div class="row" style="gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <span class="text-muted"><strong>Input:</strong> <span id="in-len">0</span> chars</span>
      <span class="text-muted"><strong>Output:</strong> <span id="out-len">0</span> chars</span>
      <span class="text-muted" id="ratio"></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>encodeURIComponent</strong> encodes every character that is not a safe URL character  — spaces become <code>%20</code>, <code>&amp;</code> becomes <code>%26</code>, and Unicode characters get UTF-8 percent-encoded.</li>
    <li><strong>encodeURI</strong> preserves URL structure  — keeps <code>:</code>, <code>/</code>, <code>?</code>, <code>=</code>, <code>&amp;</code> intact so you can paste a full URL and only the value parts get encoded.</li>
    <li><strong>Decode</strong> reverses both variants, converting any <code>%XX</code> sequence back to the original UTF-8 byte.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>About URL Encoding</h2>
  <p class="text-muted">URLs have a restricted alphabet  — only letters, digits, and a small set of punctuation can appear literally. Everything else must be percent-encoded as <code>%XX</code> where XX is the hexadecimal UTF-8 code point. When you paste a URL containing Chinese characters, spaces, or ampersands into a terminal, a query, or an HTTP header, this tool ensures every byte is represented safely. Decoding is equally useful when you're reading server logs or inspecting URL-encoded payloads from webhooks.</p>
</ToolPage>

<style>
  textarea { width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .85rem; }
</style>

<script is:inline client:load>
(function () {
  const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);
  const inField = $('input');
  const outField = $('output');

  function run() {
    const mode = $('mode').value;
    const input = inField.value;
    let output = '';
    try {
      if (mode === 'encode') output = encodeURIComponent(input);
      else if (mode === 'encodeURI') output = encodeURI(input);
      else output = decodeURIComponent(input);
    } catch (e) {
      output = 'Error: ' + e.message;
    }
    outField.value = output;
    $('in-len').textContent = input.length;
    $('out-len').textContent = output.length;
    const ratio = output.length > 0 ? ((output.length / input.length) * 100).toFixed(0) : 100;
    const txt = input.length > 0 ? (mode.startsWith('encode') ? `${ratio}% of input size` : `${ratio}% of input size`) : '';
    $('ratio').textContent = txt;
    $('stats').style.display = '';
  }

  inField.addEventListener('input', () => {
    if ($('mode').value === 'decode') run();
  });
  $('mode').addEventListener('change', run);
  $('run').addEventListener('click', run);
  $('swap').addEventListener('click', () => { inField.value = outField.value; run(); });
  $('copy').addEventListener('click', () => { navigator.clipboard.writeText(outField.value); });
  $('clear').addEventListener('click', () => { inField.value = ''; outField.value = ''; $('stats').style.display = 'none'; });
})();
</script>
